{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141885-can-you-clash-of-wills-with-yourself","id":1141885,"title":"Can you Clash of Wills with yourself?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-19T13:57:43-07:00","id":1141885,"title":"Can you Clash of Wills with yourself?","content":"I recently read Promethean, and realized that you can roll for New Dawn before completing enough Roles to make it work. In that instance you automatically fail. 2 separate Promethean powers allow you to automatically succeed at any roll. Divine Guidance lets you auto succeed at X actions, and Bulwark gives you the Steadfast condition which allows you to succeed at a roll you've already failed. Read as written I think that Steadfast would make you auto New Dawn, because your auto fail happened and then you turned it into a success. Divine Guidance auto succeeds, while New Dawn without the Roles is an auto fail, so that feels like a Clash of Wills. So the question is...can you Clash of Wills yourself?<br /> <br /> I'd also like to state that I absolutely do not think that any Player should attempt this, as it completely invalidates the whole premise of the game. But it made me think there might be other, less game abusing scenarios that could use an answer to this question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:30:14-07:00","id":1141898,"title":"","content":"Nope. There's no cheating in the Great Work. Lose 3 Pilgrimage dots, create a blighted wasteland and fall to Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T15:07:13-07:00","id":1141914,"title":"","content":"While the Great Work should be off-limits, I can inagine something like your own powers going berserk and escaping your control, but without separating from you enough to be using a separate dice pool. Or a split personality having different ideas on how to use a supernatural power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:39:15-07:00","id":1141978,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, it shouldn't be allowed. We all seem to be on the same page there. I actually have a decent answer to the original question now though: yes. There's a Beast power that redirects powers by using Clash of Wills, and you can Clash of Wills with yourself if you direct it towards, well, yourself. It seems like a decent reference point for any other self vs self ruling. Like if a vampire has a perfect recollection power, but uses another power to make himself unaware of his actions so he doesn't have to risk Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T04:10:54-07:00","id":1142457,"title":"","content":"I personally would not allow you to Clash with yourself. Like, in the case of using Auspex to check if you Domianted someone's memories well enough. You understand your own power well enough that you should be able to succeed. In the case of a Beast trying to redirect a power they themselves have control over? I'm kind of at a loss over what power they'd be firing out that they didn't already have control over, making the use redundant. In either case, I'd allow the second to succceed because, again, its your own power and you should know enough to take control without problem. This situation is rare enough that I'd just make a case-by-case ruling<br /> <br /> Now, we get to the exception. Mage. The only way to defend against Arcana is through Clash of Wills, so Mage combat generally ends up as Shielding spells Clashing against opponent spells. Its entirely concievable that you will end up with an AoE spell that that hits your allies protected by your own shielding spell (naughty mage, not getting fate 2). Which should take precidence? You're going to be trying to overwhelm opponent's shields, so its not like you can hold yourself back, but you don't want to hurt your allies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}